---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import CatStage from "../../components/CatStage.astro";
import DownloadCta from "../../components/DownloadCta.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema, languageAlternates, softwareApplicationSchema } from "../../lib/site";

const path = "/blink-reminder/";
const title = "Blink Reminder App for Mac, Windows & Linux | Lumi";
const description = "A context-aware blink reminder that detects complete blinks locally, pauses when sensing is unavailable, and asks for two slow blinks after a long gap.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  alternates={languageAlternates(path, "/zh-cn/blink-reminder/")}
  schemas={[
    softwareApplicationSchema,
    breadcrumbSchema([{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Blink reminder", path }]),
  ]}
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath={path} alternatePath="/zh-cn/blink-reminder/" />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">CONTEXT-AWARE BLINK REMINDER</p>
          <h1>Lumi detects complete blinks <span class="soft-line">and reminds you after a long gap.</span></h1>
          <p>A small prompt asks you to blink slowly twice. Completing those blinks closes the prompt and starts a cooldown.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href="/download/">Download free</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy model</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">Camera frames are processed on your computer and discarded.</p>
        </div>
        <CatStage />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="sequence-heading">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN · CLOSE · OPEN</p><h2 id="sequence-heading">How Lumi recognizes a complete blink.</h2></div>
          <p>The detector combines signals from both eyes with an eye-aspect-ratio check. It confirms a full transition and filters one-eye movement, long closure, and weak distant-face signals.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-rail">
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">01 / OBSERVE</span><h3>Confirm a usable face signal</h3><p>If confidence is low, the face is obscured, or camera access is unavailable, blink sensing pauses and the interface says why.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">02 / DETECT</span><h3>Recognize one full blink</h3><p>Both eyes need to move through a plausible open–closed–open sequence. A single uncertain frame is not enough.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">03 / RESPOND</span><h3>Mirror it with Lumi</h3><p>Lumi blinks back, making the invisible event visible without turning it into a score.</p></article>
          <article class="feature-row"><span class="feature-time">04 / NUDGE</span><h3>Invite two slow blinks after a gap</h3><p>When the configured behavior detects a long no-blink interval, a small prompt appears. Completing two blinks ends it; a cooldown limits repetition.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="pause-heading">
      <div class="shell-narrow article-body">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHEN SENSING PAUSES</p>
        <h2 id="pause-heading">The reminder waits for a usable face signal.</h2>
        <p>If you step away, block the camera, or move outside a usable range, blink sensing changes to unavailable and the no-blink interval stops. It resumes when the signal returns.</p>
        <p>Locking the screen, putting the computer to sleep, leaving the configured monitoring window, or using the master pause switch releases the camera.</p>

        <h2>What Lumi records</h2>
        <p>The local timeline stores the time of each detected complete blink. It does not store the camera frame, raw face landmarks, or an ideal blink-rate target.</p>

        <div class="article-callout">
          <strong>The blink reminder does not assess eye health</strong>
          <p>Lumi cannot diagnose dry eye disease, assess tear quality, or determine an ideal blink rate for you. Persistent or concerning eye symptoms require professional evaluation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <DownloadCta />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
